  "question": {
    "text": "A mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;connected to a horizontal spring performs S.H.M. with amplitude <math><mi>A</mi></math>.&nbsp;While mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is passing through mean position another mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is placed on it so that both the masses move together with amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
